def selection_sort(arr):
    for i in range(len(arr)):
        min_idx = i
        for j in range(i+1, len(arr)):
            if arr[j] < arr[min_idx]:
                min_idx = j
        arr[i], arr[min_idx] = arr[min_idx], arr[i]
    return arr
```

This function takes an array as input and returns an array sorted in ascending order. It uses a loop to iterate through the array, finding the minimum element in each iteration and swapping it with the element at the current index. The minimum element is then moved to the beginning of the array, and the loop is repeated until all elements have been sorted.

